      "assessment": "Full arbitrary-precision factor pipeline, shared Work counter, deterministic64-bit Miller-Rabin bases, bounded rho/trial splitting, multiplicity overflow and positive-rational factors read. u128 prevents multiplication overflow for u64 modular arithmetic; recursive prime factors are rechecked, error drops partial map. Big residual trial division maintains prime-factor condition by stripping earlier divisors. Work counts selected loop steps, not all bit operations/allocation. Complete u64 base-set theorem is a dependency, not established here by citation or inline tests. Raw BigRational invalid denominator bypasses normalized positive-rational premise; no normal constructor produces it. Sole inline test constructs literal Ok/Err and exercises no owner function.",
