      ],
      "limits": "Source reasoning only; deeper module owners pending, sibling integration tests outside this scope, no Rust execution. Mutation-count comments do not supply reproducible mutation evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "RFA-CL002",
      "statement": "For normalized rational/integer inputs, checked roots and bounded squarefree extraction compute exact identities or explicit refusal; the residual threshold is justified because all remaining prime factors exceed the trial limit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/rational.rs",
          "sha256": "49ce8730d2beb1fa9d272a1c157c963a071cd94c885bb062a70eaeaeca3527c0",
          "lines": [
            109,
            173
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/rational.rs",
          "sha256": "49ce8730d2beb1fa9d272a1c157c963a071cd94c885bb062a70eaeaeca3527c0",
          "lines": [
            215,
            327
          ]
        }
      ],
      "limits": "13,013 independent small controls,8,485 admitted and4,528 refused; exact bit complexity and unrestricted raw Ratio validity not certified. rq is explicitly partial."
    },
    {
      "id": "RFA-CL003",
      "statement": "The searched FiniteField constructor checks primality and complete bounded-degree monic-divisor irreducibility. Canonical arithmetic is polynomial quotient arithmetic; BinaryField must additionally exclude the demonstrated even-modulus and degree-zero admission gap.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/finite_field.rs",
          "sha256": "23eceeeeb33157f531554990d8b19c5e455968bc7ec3e171970c8745fde7b650",
          "lines": [
            74,
            87
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/finite_field.rs",
          "sha256": "23eceeeeb33157f531554990d8b19c5e455968bc7ec3e171970c8745fde7b650",
          "lines": [
            206,
            340
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/binary_field.rs",
          "sha256": "7549563d8b3af98d07ee7edffa4c80c7c688fb03a343e976fc96763d60ee14b9",
          "lines": [
            43,
            140
          ]
        }
      ],
      "limits": "No resource cap beyond machine cardinality; machine coefficient overflow for large primes and malformed public representations are not covered by small canonical-field controls."
    },
    {
      "id": "RFA-CL004",
      "statement": "Integer factorization uses a shared explicit work counter and exact split/primality decisions, while residue roots combine exact prime-power formulas through CRT instead of scanning all residues. Exhaustion yields a typed error without a purported complete factorization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/integer_factorization.rs",
          "sha256": "b20c3c6e53044a5f215eeac01fd8e9c3eabb0eabe2f50347f63caf838162b81f",
          "lines": [
            50,
            241
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/residue.rs",
          "sha256": "ac0e61c5c4c4376901925c11b1d08d88249c687e806b8806b206518de09a7429",
          "lines": [
            18,
            77
          ]
        }
      ],
      "limits": "Full u64 Miller-Rabin base theorem trusted as stated; finite control compares20,000 small integers, and999 residue moduli. No Rust/backend implementation run or universal complexity bound."
    },
    {
      "id": "RFA-CL005",
      "statement": "Gaussian norm verification replays submitted coordinates exactly and obstruction verification binds the input, rechecks a prime3mod4 and recomputes odd signed valuation; bounded construction separates exhaustion from non-norm. Two/four-square constructors replay positive witnesses, with a reduced-input caveat for rational norm realization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/gaussian_norm.rs",
          "sha256": "280c87abd6d873ffcd3f2c44f0c52de7cbf334073c5e2c505571080435c7c075",
          "lines": [
            108,
            206
          ]
        },
