      "limits": "Documentation inconsistency; panic is locally documented and not a failure of checked_ratio. No Rust execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "RFA-F002",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Binary field admission accepts reducible even moduli and degree zero",
      "statement": "is_irreducible_binary tries only divisors with constant term1 and never requires positive degree. BinaryField::new(2,4) therefore admits modulus x²: encoded2 is nonzero but its square is0. new(0,1) admits an order-one carrier. The constructor claim that every admitted modulus is irreducible is false.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/binary_field.rs",
          "sha256": "7549563d8b3af98d07ee7edffa4c80c7c688fb03a343e976fc96763d60ee14b9",
          "lines": [
            44,
            61
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/binary_field.rs",
          "sha256": "7549563d8b3af98d07ee7edffa4c80c7c688fb03a343e976fc96763d60ee14b9",
          "lines": [
            85,
            98
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/binary_field.rs",
          "sha256": "7549563d8b3af98d07ee7edffa4c80c7c688fb03a343e976fc96763d60ee14b9",
          "lines": [
            129,
            140
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/binary_field.rs",
          "sha256": "7549563d8b3af98d07ee7edffa4c80c7c688fb03a343e976fc96763d60ee14b9",
          "lines": [
            349,
            374
          ]
        }
      ],
      "limits": "Independent mask model,127 polynomials degree<=6:23 false admissions including the constant1 case. Standard first-irreducible search starts odd and valid degrees1..4 retained sound bounded arithmetic checks. No source execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "RFA-F003",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Public field elements are not admitted to their carrier",
      "statement": "FieldElement.coeffs is public; even a searched valid GF4 accepts [] beside [1,0], with add returning [] by zip and trace_value subsequently indexing an empty sum. Longer vectors can index past product. No length, coefficient range or field identity is checked.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/finite_field.rs",
          "sha256": "23eceeeeb33157f531554990d8b19c5e455968bc7ec3e171970c8745fde7b650",
